  "history": {
   "value": "Battery Ventures was founded in Boston in 1983 by Rick Frisbie, Howard Anderson and Bob Barrett. It backed Akamai, FORE Systems and the companies that became Nextel, and later Coinbase, Databricks, Wayfair and Datadog. One fund family makes its seed, growth and buyout investments, so the track record on this page covers its minority stakes only; it raised $3.25B for Fund XV in 2026.",
